        "created_at": "2018-08-26T19:43:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Hey all! Trying to figure out the correct ruling on a couple card interactions. The general theme:&nbsp;<span>If Stuntman is made immune to damage (Meteor Storm, Heroic Interception, Ground Pound, etc.), does that trigger a power usage from Moving Target?</span></p><p>My instinct: No. The damage is not being reduced, redirected, or prevented, it is being stopped by immunity, and therefore the card conditions are unfulfilled and he gets no power usage.</p><p>My group's instinct: immunity counts as a \"prevention\" and so he gets a power usage.</p><p>No game hinges on this (the damage his power usage would have caused would have just come from somewhere else, we'd just have planned our turns a bit differently) but I want to play it honestly.</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
        "post_number": 1,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:51:45.762Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
