        "bookmarked": false,
        "raw": "<p>Hey all! Trying to figure out the correct ruling on a couple card interactions. The general theme:&nbsp;<span style=\"font-size: 13px;\">If Stuntman is made immune to damage (Meteor Storm, Heroic Interception, Ground Pound, etc.), does that trigger a power usage from Moving Target?</span></p><p>My instinct: No. The damage is not being reduced, redirected, or prevented, it is being stopped by immunity, and therefore the card conditions are unfulfilled and he gets no power usage.</p><p>My group&#39;s instinct: immunity counts as a &quot;prevention&quot; and so he gets a power usage.</p><p>No game hinges on this (the damage his power usage would have caused would have just come from somewhere else, we&#39;d just have planned our turns a bit differently) but I want to play it honestly.</p><p>Thanks!</p>",
